hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15591","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Malik, that Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to him, he said: I saw al-Saib smelling his garment. I said to him: What is that for? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No wudu except from wind or sound."
